{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2ba7ffe864355d19","name":"G-Type Light Shuttle","source":{"id":"source:reference-2ba7ffe864355d19","title":"G-Type Light Shuttle","revision":19141,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:23:46Z","sha256":"737a6bfdec62bdb9d65c24064f7d24ee0a8e9bcaa54991765cd5c9d41fa74d9e","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19141","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=G-Type%20Light%20Shuttle&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2ba7ffe864355d19","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Hoersch-Kessel Drive G-Type Light Shuttle is a small spacecraft designed to ferry individuals and small groups from orbiting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," down to the surface of a planet. The 23-meter-long G-Type Shuttle is also designed to be easy to pilot, and it has an exceptionally sophisticated pilot assistance system that allows even rookie pilots to make it safely from space to surface. As a result, characters who are not ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trained"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained"}," in the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," skill gain a +2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Pilot","referenceId":"reference:383e2d946278a872"}," checks in a G-Type Light Shuttle. The pilot assistance software package offers no benefit to experienced pilots.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Lightly armed, the G-Type Light Shuttle is somewhat more fragile than other transport ships and rarely sees use in combat scenarios. G-Type Light Shuttles are lightweight and nimble, though, and many have found their way into the hands of smugglers and other less-than-reputable individuals who use the ships to avoid law enforcement entanglements.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Unlike other shuttlecraft (such as the ",{"tag":"a","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Ministry"]},"-Class Orbital Shuttle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ministry-Class_Orbital_Shuttle","referenceId":"reference:9c38399c5bef52f1"},"), the G-Type Light Shuttle has a limited passenger capacity. An alternative configuration (colloquially referred to as the ",{"tag":"a","children":["G-Type Escape Shuttle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/G-Type_Escape_Shuttle","referenceId":"reference:74f04272cd36d113"},") accommodates only a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," with no passengers.  The passenger space is used for extra shielding in this model. Additionally, the Escape Shuttle variant boasts a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," and enough supplies for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," to survive several months. The advanced pilot-assistance software enables politicians and other VIPs with no experience in the cockpit of a Starship to escape war zones and reach safer worlds.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["G-Type Light Shuttle Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","childre